%% 09 Enforcement approval and guards. P0 stops at dry-run; apply is P1 and needs human-confirmed pf spike.
sequenceDiagram
  actor Admin
  participant A as sentinel-api
  participant V as validator
  participant R as pf renderer
  participant D as sentineld
  A->>V: proposal from structured incident fields (never LLM text)
  V->>V: safelist (gateway, admin, config hosts)
  V->>V: lockout (API client IP/MAC)
  V->>V: TTL required and <= max
  V->>V: blast radius (max hosts blocked)
  V-->>A: reject with reason (audit entry) or accept
  A->>R: render rule text from fields
  R-->>A: exact pf text (dry run result)
  A-->>Admin: show dry run
  Admin->>A: approve (GUI/CLI)
  Note over A,D: P1 only, after HUMAN_VERIFICATION pf spike confirmed
  A->>D: apply into anchor "sentinel" via Unix socket
  D-->>A: result
  A->>A: audit apply, schedule expiry
  D-->>A: TTL expiry removes rule (audit)
  Admin->>A: revoke / revoke --all
  A->>D: remove
